{"gene":"CDK4","uniprot":"P11802","proteinName":"cyclin-dependent kinase 4","function":"Ser/Thr-kinase component of cyclin D-CDK4 (DC) complexes that phosphorylate and inhibit members of the retinoblastoma (RB) protein family including RB1 and regulate the cell-cycle during G(1)/S transition. Phosphorylation of RB1 allows dissociation of the transcription factor E2F from the RB/E2F complexes and the subsequent transcription of E2F target genes which are responsible for the progression through the G(1) phase. Hypophosphorylates RB1 in early G(1) phase. Cyclin D-CDK4 complexes are major integrators of various mitogenenic and antimitogenic signals. Also phosphorylates SMAD3 in a cell-cycle-dependent manner and represses its transcriptional activity. Component of the ternary complex, cyclin D/CDK4/CDKN1B, required for nuclear translocation and activity of the cyclin D-CDK4 complex","pathwayComment":null,"pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-9687139","name":"Aberrant regulation of mitotic cell cycle due to RB1 defects","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9659787","name":"Aberrant regulation of mitotic G1/S transition in cancer due to RB1 defects","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1280218","name":"Adaptive Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9843745","name":"Adipogenesis","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-69278","name":"Cell Cycle, Mitotic","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2262752","name":"Cellular responses to stress","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2559583","name":"Cellular Senescence","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-3247509","name":"Chromatin modifying enzymes","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-389948","name":"Co-inhibition by PD-1","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-69656","name":"Cyclin A:Cdk2-associated events at S phase entry","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9675132","name":